{
  "note": "🧺️ Action sets of a plugin manifest: a plugin declares an action table once and every app it names receives the rows in table order, ahead of its own roster. `resolution` cases give each app's own roster and the sets; `resolved` is the roster each app resolves to (the windows' app roster) and `fault` the one reason the table is refused, or null when it is sound. `sharing` cases give each app's declared roster and the sets a plugin forms in order, each over the apps named in `members`: `sets` is the table that results (id, member apps, rows), `remaining` what is left on each roster and `refusal` why a set cannot be formed. Every language resolves and validates the same table to the same answer.",
